*Edit:* That being said, your comment from #83042 is correct, the `EditorNode` code could call `OS::get_singleton()->set_exit_code(EXIT_FAILURE)` when it's completely failing the export. It's less clean than communicating back to `Main` and letting it handle the error code, but it can be done.

But that again is independent from the changes in this PR, it can be done against current `master` and backported to `4.2`.

*Edit 2:* Actually the EditorNode code already takes care of setting the exit code on failure, though `_exit_editor(EXIT_FAILURE)`. But for some reason that doesn't work (most likely other code that runs in parallel / afterwards in `main.cpp`/`os_<platform>` overrides it).

